    <item>
      <title>Common Algorithm Patterns</title>
      <link>https://yy-tech.online/post/common-algorithm-patterns/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 27 May 2026 22:02:00 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://yy-tech.online/post/common-algorithm-patterns/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;common-algorithm-patterns&#34;&gt;Common Algorithm Patterns&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each pattern has only two parts: &lt;strong&gt;Explanation&lt;/strong&gt; + &lt;strong&gt;Code Framework&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;1-framework-thinking-traversal-first&#34;&gt;1) Framework Thinking (Traversal First)&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;explanation&#34;&gt;Explanation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Most problems are traversal problems in disguise: arrays, linked lists, trees, graphs.&lt;br&gt;
Identify the data structure first, then pick traversal order, then fill business logic into the skeleton.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;code-framework&#34;&gt;Code Framework&lt;/h3&gt;
